            <exercise workspace="3in">
                <title>The Jacobian</title>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        <ol>
                            <li>
                                <p>
                                    For a transformation <m>x=g(u,v)</m> and <m>y=h(u,v)</m>, the <term>Jacobian</term> 
                                    is the expression
                                    
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    <m>\displaystyle J = </m>
                                </p>
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <p>
                                    For a transformation <m>x=g(u,v,w)</m>, <m>y=h(u,v,w)</m>, and <m>z=k(u,v,w)</m> the <term>Jacobian</term> 
                                    is the expression
                                    
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    <m>\displaystyle J = x_u(y_vz_w - y_wz_v) - x_v(y_uz_w - y_wz_u) + x_w(y_uz_v -y_vz_u) </m>
                                </p>
                            </li>
                        </ol>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </exercise>

